    "willem": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Open with Willem (SPEC.md at 3f88252):\n\n1. Default books no loss: LoanManage uses TotalValueOutstanding, which is 0 on a confidential loan, so the vault's share price ignores loan B and the last depositor to redeem takes the shortfall. How should a default write it off?\n\n2. Does ConfidentialLoanPay clear impairment, as LoanPay does?\n\n3. Who holds the Loan Auditor key? Proposal: reuse the MPT Auditor key.\n\nAnswered: LoanSet, ConfidentialLoanPay and LoanBrokerSettle fields and proofs; the settled amount is public; interest reaches the vault as settle above DebtTotal; a regular payment moves NextPaymentDueDate by one PaymentInterval; overpayment (a payment is at least the Periodic Payment and at most the Amount Owed); settle timing (the broker can settle at any time, after merging the Lending Balance inbox).",
      "w": 440,
      "x": 1840,
      "y": 0
    },
